<header><p class="st-kicker">tribal confederation · France and the Low Countries</p><h1 class="st-title">Treveri</h1><p class="st-meta">300 BCE – 51 BCE (approx.) · capital Titelberg</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Powerful people of the Moselle, famed for their cavalry, whose land became the site of Trier, a Roman imperial capital.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Treveri lived along the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moselle">Moselle</a> in modern <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/county-of-luxembourg">Luxembourg</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhineland-palatinate">Rhineland-Palatinate</a>. They were counted among the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/belgae-britain">Belgae</a>, though <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tacitus">Tacitus</a> says they claimed Germanic descent. Their great oppidum on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/titelberg">Titelberg</a> in Luxembourg was a centre of minting and trade.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Caesar calls their cavalry the best in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gaul">Gaul</a>. Their nobility split between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indutiomarus">Indutiomarus</a>, leader of the anti-Roman party, and his son-in-law <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cingetorix-treveri">Cingetorix</a>, who backed Caesar.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indutiomarus">Indutiomarus</a> led a revolt in 54 BCE and was killed; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/titus-labienus">Labienus</a> defeated the Treveri in 53 BCE. Around 16 BCE the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Romans</a> founded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/trier">Augusta Treverorum</a> (Trier), which became the capital of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/gallic-empire">Gallic Empire</a> and of the western <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/roman-empire">Roman Empire</a> under Constantine.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/treveri.jpg" alt="Treveri" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: Roßbacher at German Wikipedia · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bund-ro-altburg.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>300 BCE – 51 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/4th-century-bce">4th century BCE</a> – <a href="/centuries/1st-century-bce">1st century BCE</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>tribal confederation</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Titelberg</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Indutiomarus, Cingetorix</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Celtic polytheism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Gaulish</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/germany">Germany</a>, <a href="/countries/luxembourg">Luxembourg</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Treviri</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=-176&amp;focus=treveri" aria-label="Treveri on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4815 452 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Treveri lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5135 708L5304 942"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5304 942h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5135 708h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5135 708h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Titelberg. <a href="/atlas?year=-176&amp;focus=treveri">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

